# Wave W17-U (Route 202): gate oak — an approach oak in mature deep greens, broad-crowned over the city road with the highlight lifted clear of the turf, on gate turf (ground baked in; renamed in-plan — the draft gateelm is a shipped kind). Route 202’s own tree — older and deeper than Route 201’s young shore elm beside it, and split from Route 203’s dusted coal pine by form entire (broadleaf avenue vs conifer mine country).
